      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Let the weight of one bowling ball be x pounds. Let the weight of one canoe be y pounds.\nWe are given that seven bowling balls weigh the same as three canoes, so:\n7x = 3y\n\nWe are also given that two canoes weigh a total of 56 pounds, so:\n2y = 56\n\nWe can solve this system of equations by eliminating one of the variables. Let's solve the second equation for y:\ny = 56/2 = 28\n\nNow we can substitute this value of y into the first equation:\n7x = 3(28) = 84\n\nTo find the value of x, we divide both sides of the equation by 7:\nx = 84/7 = 12\n\nTherefore, one bowling ball weighs 12 pounds. The final answer is $\\boxed{12}$.",
