    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the weight of one bowling ball based on the given information about the canoes. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Define Variables:**\n   - Let \\( b \\) represent the weight of one bowling ball in pounds.\n   - Let \\( c \\) represent the weight of one canoe in pounds.\n\n   Given:\n   - Seven bowling balls weigh the same as three canoes:\n     \\[\n     7b = 3c\n     \\]\n\n   - Two canoes weigh a total of 56 pounds:\n     \\[\n     2c = 56\n     \\]\n\n2. **Solve for \\( c \\):**\n   - We simplify the second equation to find \\( c \\):\n     \\[\n     c = \\frac{56}{2} = 28\n     \\]\n\n3. **Substitute \\( c \\) into the first equation:**\n   - We substitute \\( c = 28 \\) into \\( 7b = 3c \\):\n     \\[\n     7b = 3 \\times 28\n     \\]\n\n   - Calculate the right-hand side:\n     \\[\n     7b = 84\n     \\]\n\n4. **Solve for \\( b \\):**\n   - Divide both sides by 7 to find \\( b \\):\n     \\[\n     b = \\frac{84}{7} = 12\n     \\]\n\nConclusion:\nThe weight of one bowling ball is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]",
